	<section class="sec-product-detail">
		<div class="inner">
			<h2 class="ttl-comp03 mbpc-59 mbsp-30" id="anc01">
				Super Insulation
			</h2>
			<div class="main-content">
				<div class="insulation-sub txt-center mbpc-62 mbsp-30">
					<img src="/en/products/heat-measures/images/insulation/insulation-sub1.jpg" alt="Super Insulation">
				</div>
				<div class="flex_content mbpc-68 mbsp-30">
					<div class="flex_content__left w60p_pc">
						<p>
							This is a vacuum multilayer heat insulating material used as a radiation heat suppression film in vacuum areas for cryogenic and space applications. It demonstrates good thermal insulation performance as a cryogenic MLI* for equipment used near absolute zero, such as superconducting equipment, superconducting power transmission cables, and cryogenic containers, and as a thermal shield to protects satellites and spacecraft from radiant heat. MLI has been used in many space applications, including the “KOUNOTORI” Space Station supply vehicle and the “KIBO” International Space Station.<br>
							<span>*MLI: Multi-Layer Insulation</span>
						</p>
					</div>
					<div class="flex_content__right">
						<img src="/en/products/heat-measures/images/insulation/insulation-sub2.jpg" alt="Super Insulation">
					</div>
				</div>
				<h3 class="ttl-comp04 mbpc-40 mbsp-30">Features</h3>
				<ul class="contract-list txt-basic mbpc-69">
					<li class="contract-list__item">
						Integrated production from raw material polyimide film  APICAL&trade; in KANEKA.
					</li>
					<li class="contract-list__item">
						Good heat insulating properties as a vacuum insulation material for cryogenic temperature cryostats
					</li>
					<li class="contract-list__item">
						Protects the spacecraft and satellites from radiation heat
					</li>
					<li class="contract-list__item">
						Proven track record in space applications such as H-II Transfer Vehicle “Kounotori”(JAXA) and International Space Station "Kibo" missions
					</li>
				</ul>
				<h3 class="ttl-comp04 mbpc-40 mbsp-30">Applications</h3>
				<ul class="list-dots mbpc-63 mbsp-30">
					<li>Multi Layer insulation for superconducting equipment</li>
					<li>Multi Layer insulation for cryogenic containers</li>
					<li>Multi Layer insulation for space use</li>
				</ul>
				<h3 class="ttl-comp04 mbpc-40 mbsp-30">Related Sites</h3>
				<ul class="list-dots mbpc-67 mbsp-30">
					<li><a href="https://www.tochigi-kaneka.co.jp/" target="_blank" class="c_blue">Tochigi Kaneka Corporation</a></li>
				</ul>
			</div>
		</div>
		<div class="dot-line"></div>
		<div class="inner">
			<h2 class="ttl-comp03 mbpc-50 mbsp-30" id="anc02">Thermal Strap for Space Applications</h2>
			<div class="main-content">
				<div class="flex_content mbpc-50 mbsp-30">
					<div class="flex_content__left w60p_pc">
						<div class="txt-lead">
							This is a heat transport material, using multi-layered graphite sheets, to cool heat-generating parts of satellites.<br>
							Compared to copper and aluminum, this material has a high heat transport capacity and it is lightweight, flexible and bendable.
						</div>
					</div>
					<div class="flex_content__right w35p_pc">
						<img src="/en/products/heat-measures/images/graphite-sheet/img-17.jpg" class="w100p mbpc-10 mbsp-10" alt="Graphite Thermal Strap">
					</div>
				</div>
				<h3 class="ttl-comp04 mbpc-40 mbsp-30">Features</h3>
				<ul class="contract-list txt-basic">
					<li class="contract-list__item">
						Multilayer graphite sheet allows for high heat transport (GS) (3 times higher thermal conductivity than copper)
					</li>
					<li class="contract-list__item">
						Light weight (density 1.8 g/cm³) 　→　1/5 of copper, 2/3 of aluminum
					</li>
					<li class="contract-list__item">
						Flexible and bendable
					</li>
					<li class="contract-list__item">
						Low outgas, suitable for outer space use
					</li>
				</ul>
				<h3 class="ttl-comp04 mbpc-40 mbsp-30">Applications</h3>
				<ul class="list-dots mbpc-40 mbsp-30">
					<li>Space applications, mainly cooling of heat-generating components of satellites</li>
				</ul>
				<h3 class="ttl-comp04 mbpc-40 mbsp-30">Related Sites</h3>
				<ul class="list-dots mbpc-40 mbsp-30">
					<li><a href="https://www.tochigi-kaneka.co.jp/" target="_blank" class="c_blue">Tochigi Kaneka Corporation</a></li>
				</ul>
			</div>
		</div>		
	</section>
